{
  "headline": "FDA's records trace our supply to a plant classified OAI 596 days before the shortage posting",
  "headline_cites": ["D12"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "FDA first posted the midazolam hydrochloride shortage on 2020-04-02 and it remains current as of 2026-10-21.",
      "cites": ["E59", "D23"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Our Corvale East and Corvale General sites both stock the 1 mg/mL 5 mL vial labeled by Hospira, Inc. (NDC 00409230505).",
      "cites": ["E2", "E8"]
    },
    {
      "text": "That label identifies two registered plants: Hospira, Inc. (FEI 1021343) and Pfizer Healthcare India Private Limited (FEI 3008316085).",
      "cites": ["E22", "E34", "E43"]
    },
    {
      "text": "FDA inspection 1064827 at the Hospira plant (FEI 1925262) ended 2018-08-15 and was classified OAI, 596 days before the shortage posting.",
      "cites": ["D12", "E30"]
    },
    {
      "text": "FDA inspection 1106244 at the Pfizer India plant ended 2019-09-06 and was classified OAI, 209 days before the shortage posting.",
      "cites": ["D14", "E40"]
    },
    {
      "text": "A Warning Letter was issued to the Pfizer India plant on 2020-03-25, 8 days before the shortage posting.",
      "cites": ["D18", "E42"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The highest-ranked mitigation is to transfer 6 vials of 1 mg/mL 5 mL from Corvale East to Corvale General, which would raise Corvale General from 9.9 to 11 days on hand while Corvale East remains above two weeks.",
      "cites": ["D24"]
    }
  ]
}
